# Qt / QML Style Rules

Author: slspencer
Copyright: 2026

## Scope

Applies to `.qml`, `.cpp`, `.h`, and Qt integration files.

## Rules

- Keep UI behavior declarative in QML where practical.
- Keep heavy logic out of QML and in Rust/C++ controllers.
- Ensure signal/slot naming remains clear and consistent.
- Use absolute path handling when resolving local files.
- Prefer reusable UI components over duplicated inline blocks.

## Maintainability

- Keep bindings reactive and avoid hidden side effects.
- Document non-trivial UI state transitions.
